Title: The Conservatory
Order: 7
Production Code: 1x07

INT. VANCE ESTATE - CONSERVATORY - DAY

AMB: a garden party murmuring in the next room

[[Reuel Briggs]] leads [[Dianthe Lusk]] away from the crush of admirers to the quiet of the conservatory.

Away from the music in the next room, he tells his love and asks his fate. She looks at his plain face, at the stalwart elegance of his figure, and into his dark, true, clever eyes.

DIANTHE LUSK
(a sigh like a tired child's)
Yes.

She creeps into his arms. [[Aubrey Livingston]] finds them there when the company has gone. The wedding is set for June.

INT. LIVINGSTON'S ROOMS - NIGHT

AMB: a low fire

One March evening. Reuel, almost penniless, comes to [[Aubrey Livingston]] for help — every position he's applied for has mysteriously fallen through.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
Briggs — do you think anyone knows or suspects your origin?

REUEL BRIGGS
(steady)
I've wondered if that's the reason.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
This prejudice closes doors in good men's faces. I'm ashamed of my own section for it.

(beat)

There's an English expedition sailing for Meroe. They need a physician who isn't afraid of ruins. Two years' contract, and a fortune in it if it goes well — and some good it might do the race, if the histories it's chasing turn out true.

REUEL BRIGGS
(faintly)
But Dianthe!

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
Don't I know how I would feel if it were Molly and I in your place? You will choose love and poverty, I suppose. I should.

Reuel says nothing. He goes home and paces the cheerless room all night; by morning he has decided.

INT. LIVINGSTON'S ROOMS - MORNING

AMB: coffee steaming at the breakfast table

REUEL BRIGGS
I shall ask you to watch over Dianthe. I intrust her to you as I would intrust her to my brother, had I one.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
Between us, Reuel, oaths are useless. Molly and I will have her with us always like a dear sister.

They clasp hands on it. Neither says what either one is actually thinking.
